apaTables bundles the apaquarto Quarto extension in
inst/_extensions/wjschne/apaquarto/.

apaquarto
  Copyright (c) W. Joel Schneider
  https://github.com/wjschne/apaquarto
  License: CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
  CC0 requires no attribution; the author is nonetheless credited in
  the Authors@R field of DESCRIPTION with the 'ctb' role as a courtesy ('cph' would
  be inaccurate -- a CC0 dedication retains no copyright to hold).
  Local modifications are listed in
  inst/_extensions/wjschne/apaquarto/PATCHES.md. The bundled Word reference
  document apaquarto.docx is modified too; it is binary, so the changes to it do
  not appear in that diff: the Table style in it sets 10 pt type, six cloned
  table styles (Table6 to Table9, Table11, Table12) carry the other sizes
  that apatablesize.lua selects per table, a paragraph style (ApaTableRule)
  draws the rule under a column spanner, and the fixed cell padding of every
  table style is cut from 58 to 15 twips per side. These modifications are
  carried in this package only; they have not been contributed back to the
  upstream project.

apa.csl (inst/_extensions/wjschne/apaquarto/apa.csl)
  Copyright (c) Brenton M. Wiernik
  From the Citation Style Language project, https://citationstyles.org/
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported
           https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
  ATTRIBUTION IS A CONDITION OF THIS LICENSE, unlike the CC0 dedication
  above, so the author is named here AND credited in the
  Authors@R field of DESCRIPTION with 'ctb' and 'cph' roles. The style file names him in an
  <author> element.
  Included unmodified. It cannot be omitted: the apaquarto filter citeprocr.lua calls
  citeproc unconditionally, so a document with no citations at all fails to
  render without it.
